  "reason": "With no completed experiments, there is zero evidence to guide exploitation, so the priority is establishing a clean, interpretable baseline. config_006 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50, no aggregation, no fusion) is the simplest and most standard single-modality configuration: it uses the most widely adopted image encoder (ResNet-50), the least complex profile setting, and introduces no confounding aggregation or fusion steps. This gives a clear reference performance for the image modality alone. All subsequent experiments—adding RNA (multimodal), switching to multiprofile, changing the image encoder, or testing fusion strategies—can be directly compared against this anchor. Choosing a more complex multimodal or multiprofile configuration first would conflate multiple design decisions and make it impossible to attribute performance to any single choice, wasting the limited budget."
}

